    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "edit.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Add is_insert on impl Edit. The body is one condition: self.old.is_empty() && !self.new.is_empty(). Do not nest an if inside an if. Do not touch insert, delete, old_end, new_end, delta, invert, or overlaps. The existing test overlapping_edits_are_rejected_at_construction stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test an_insert_has_no_old_text checks Edit::insert of Offset(0) and ab is true. Edit::delete of Offset(0) and ab is false. An Edit with old a and new b is false. An Edit with old and new both empty is false. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
